Backport of upstream 4645e241a8 ("testsuites/psxstat: Expect statvfs() on IMFS
to succeed"), 2026-07-29, already in origin/main.

Not a local fix.  It is here only because the src/rtems pin is 139 commits
behind origin/main and sits between the two upstream commits that have to
travel together:

  e618b20215  2025-06-11  gave IMFS a real .statvfs_h that returns 0
  4645e241a8  2026-07-29  updated psxstat, which still expected ENOSYS

Between those two, psxstat fails on every BSP, which is what our pin does.
Drop this patch the moment the pin moves past 4645e241a8; keeping it after
that will make apply_patches.sh report it as already applied, which is
harmless but misleading.

The .scn hunk of the upstream commit is omitted deliberately.  Nothing
compares .scn files -- see CLAUDE.md -- and carrying it would only widen the
diff against the pin.

diff --git a/testsuites/psxtests/psxstat/test.c b/testsuites/psxtests/psxstat/test.c
index 0f730c1109..e7fae78819 100644
--- a/testsuites/psxtests/psxstat/test.c
+++ b/testsuites/psxtests/psxstat/test.c
@@ -785,10 +785,9 @@ void test_statvfs( void )
   status = mkdir( "/tmp", 0777 );
   rtems_test_assert( status == 0 );
 
-  puts( "statvfs, with valid path - expect ENOSYS" );
+  puts( "statvfs, with valid path - expect success" );
   status = statvfs( "/tmp", &stat );
-  rtems_test_assert( status == -1 );
-  rtems_test_assert( errno == ENOSYS );
+  rtems_test_assert( status == 0 );
 
   puts( "statvfs tested!" );
 }
